    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπλοια</span></b> , ἡ, 
			Ion.
		 and poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπλοΐη</span></b> ,
			<i><span class="en">
			Call.
			<u>Dian.</u>
			230
		</span></i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			7.640
		</span></i> (Antip.). <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπλους</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>impossibility of sailing, detention in port,</i> esp. from
			stress of weather, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				188
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπλοίᾳ χρῆσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					88
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IT</u>
				15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡσύχαζεν ὑπὸ ἀπλοίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				6.22
			</span></i>: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποπλέειν . . ὁρμημένον αὐτὸν ἶσχον
					ἄπλοιαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.119
				</span></i>
			.</div>
